Format Version="2010"
Display Name="NI Current Value Table"


[Description]
Description="Machine control, automation, and application monitoring are typically all developed as independent processes running on one or more systems. Each process performs a distinct task but share a set of common data or variables which allow successful completion of all application tasks.\0D\0A\0D\0AThe Current Value Table (CVT) serves as the central data component and can be used in a wide range of applications. It allows application components to share a common data repository and have direct access to the most up-to-date value of any variable used between components. Using this architecture, one component in the application can handle all of the I/O operations, for example, and share the I/O data variables or tags with other application components. Application operations such as alarm detection, user interface updates, process logic, etc. can then be handled by separate processes, sharing the same data repository.\0D\0A\0D\0AThe CVT implementation is a two layer hierarchy consisting of core VIs and API VIs. The core contains all the functionality of the CVT, including the data storage mechanism and additional service functions. The API VIs provide access to the CVT functionality. You can choose from three groups of API functions that each provide slightly different access to the CVT and vary in flexibility, performance, and ease-of-use.\0D\0A\0D\0ASystem Requirements\0D\0AApplication Software: LabVIEW Full Development System 2010 or later\0D\0A\0D\0ADetailed Description: Current Value Table (CVT) Reference Library\0D\0Ahttp://zone.ni.com/devzone/cda/epd/p/id/5326\0D\0A\0D\0ASupport for Current Value Table Reference Library\0D\0Ahttp://forums.ni.com/t5/Components/Current-Value-Table-CVT/m-p/583424"
Summary="Reference Library for Current Value Table, a global data storage and retrieval mechanism"
License="NI Sample Code License"
Copyright="Copyright (c) 2013, National Instruments"
Distribution=""
Vendor="National Instruments"
URL=""
Packager="National Instruments"
Demo="FALSE"
Release Notes="Added support for array data types.\0D\0A\0D\0AFixed bug where Read and Write functions could attempt to access the wrong index if the CVT was cleared and reinitialized after Read and Write functions are called such that a tag with the same name is present at a different index.\0D\0A\0D\0AIf Read/Write Index or Static Read/Write functions are used, this fix is not present to preserve maximum performance on these functions.  If using these functions, do not reinitialize the CVT with a differently-ordered set of tags without resetting the entire application."
System Package="FALSE"
Sub Package="FALSE"
License Agreement="TRUE"


